README.md:11:- Handing a saved epic to Linear: [`docs/runbooks/linear-transfer.md`](docs/runbooks/linear-transfer.md)
README.md:27:10. **Hand off to Linear** — instead of running an epic here, press **Transfer to Linear** to move its saved plan, once, to a Linear project in execution order. An agent with Linear's own MCP server creates the project, milestones and issues and reads them back; a read-back that matches the plan completes the epic. Runs and Save are locked while the transfer is open. See [Transfer an epic to Linear](docs/runbooks/linear-transfer.md).
docs/runbooks/mcp-setup.md:238:The whole flow, from the app's Transfer to Linear button to what completion records, is in [Transfer an epic to Linear](linear-transfer.md).

